{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Health and Happiness", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Be Supposed To </span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:  <br/> <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">To be</span> + <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span> + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We are <span class=\"strong\">supposed to take care of</span> not only our physical health but also our emotional health.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**: <br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. <br/> <br/> Like this: Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sadness isn't supposed to make you sick.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "These chemicals are supposed to be released when one is suffering from anxiety.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We are supposed to take care of not only our physical health but also our emotional health.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modals for Suggestions, Necessity and Possibility", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use modals to talk about degrees of certainty, possibility and necessity.</p><p>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. </p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">suggestions</span> are: <br/><span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">can</span> and <span class=\"italic\">should</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">could take </span>some medicine to feel better.<br/>You <span class=\"strong\">should get </span>some rest before a test.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">necessity</span> are: <br/><span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Teachers <span class=\"strong\">have to consider </span>the impact that stress has on students' performance.  <br/>Students <span class=\"strong\">must also take </span>good care of their physical and mental health if they want academic success.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">possibility </span>are: <br/><span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may </span>and <span class=\"italic\">might</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'm so sad, I <span class=\"strong\">might get </span>the flu.<br/>Recent research has shown that there <span class=\"strong\">could be </span>a direct link between people's emotional state and their physical well-being. </span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "complex ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "complicated; difficult to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The teacher knew little about the complex human body.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear/use to talk about physical and emotional health.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pupil ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a student, usually in elementary or primary school", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A pupil was disappointed in her grades.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "link ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a connection", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There could be a direct link between physical and emotional health.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "well-being ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "good state of health and happiness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People's emotional state is supposed to be related to their physical well-being.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "immune system", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the different components of the body that need to work together to keep a person's good health", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Anxiety caused before a final exam might affect a person's immune system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "degree ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "level; grade", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The degree of activity of white blood cells was lower.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "white blood cell", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the microscopic components of your body that help to fight diseases", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: White blood cells had a lower activity on an exam day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "academic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to school subjects that teach intellectual skills", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For academic success, students must take care of their physical and mental health.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online and find 10 idioms about health and/or happiness. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write them down and choose your favorites.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share them with a partner. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner to guess the meaning of your favorite idioms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to use them in conversation.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I identify idioms about health and happiness.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I choose my favorite idioms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share them with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about health and happiness.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn8le12ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "A ten-year-old pupil who was disappointed in her grades responded to her report card by saying, \"I'm so sad, I might get the flu.\" The teacher's reply was, \"Don't be silly. Sadness isn't supposed to make you sick.\" It may be that the teacher knew less about the complex human body than her pupil. <br/>\nRecent research has shown that there could be a direct link between people's emotional state and their physical well-being."}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob07re2img02.jpg", "time": "26500", "id": 2, "text": "Research conducted at a University in Ohio showed that anxiety caused before a final exam of medical students affected their immune system. The degree of activity of the cells that fight disease (white blood cells) was much lower on the day of the exam. Another research project showed that college students who felt lonely or upset had three times less activity of the white blood cells.<br/>\nIt seems that certain chemicals from the brain can lower the power of the immune system. These chemicals are supposed to be released when one is suffering from anxiety. If this explanation is supported by further research, our teacher will be proven wrong. An upset pupil would certainly be more likely to get the flu!"}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob07re2img03.jpg", "time": "70750", "id": 3, "text": "What does this mean? We are supposed to take care not only of our physical health but also our emotional health. Teachers have to consider the impact that stress has on students' performance. Students must also take good care of their physical and mental health if they want academic success."}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le12ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le12ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about staying healthy.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express possibility and certainty.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How do you feel before a big test or interview? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you think that there is a connection between stress and illness? What's the connection?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Can studying make you sick?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Let's read about the link between stress and health. What is the impact of <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">anxiety</span> on the brain?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"con